Expose Arrow-native result collection through the C API

Adds two functions (see duckdb-arrow-collector-request.md for the upstream
feature request this implements):

  - duckdb_pending_prepared_arrow(stmt, rows_per_batch, &pending): plans the
    prepared statement with DuckDB's PhysicalArrowCollector selected, so
    execution assembles Arrow record batches directly instead of materializing
    data chunks that a second pass converts.
  - duckdb_result_arrow_array_stream(&result, &stream): moves the collected
    batches out of the executed result into a caller-provided Arrow C stream
    interface ArrowArrayStream.

Note for upstreaming: duckdb.h is autogenerated by scripts/generate_c_api.py;
this patch edits the generated header directly, an upstream PR must add the
definitions to src/include/duckdb/main/capi/header_generation/ instead.

